<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>A Step-by-Step Guide to Effective Feature Prioritization</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Effective feature prioritization helps product teams determine which
                    features should be developed first based on customer value, business
                    impact, effort, risk, and strategic objectives. A structured approach
                    ensures that limited development resources are focused on the highest-value
                    opportunities.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Collect Feature Requests:</b> Gather ideas and requirements from customers, stakeholders, sales teams, support teams, product analytics, and market research.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Understand Customer Value:</b> Evaluate how strongly each feature addresses customer problems, needs, and expectations.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Evaluate Business Impact:</b> Consider the potential contribution of each feature to revenue, growth, retention, efficiency, or strategic objectives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Estimate Development Effort:</b> Work with technical teams to understand complexity, resources, dependencies, and expected delivery effort.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Assess Risk:</b> Identify technical, operational, security, compliance, and market risks associated with each feature.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Score and Rank Features:</b> Use a consistent prioritization framework to compare features objectively.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Create the Product Roadmap:</b> Place prioritized features into appropriate development stages and release plans.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Review Regularly:</b> Revisit priorities as customer needs, business objectives, market conditions, and product data change.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant feature prioritization image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-4">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Key Critical Factors for Successful Feature Prioritization</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Strong feature prioritization requires a balance between customer
                    expectations, business objectives, technical feasibility, and available
                    resources. Clear evaluation criteria help teams make consistent and
                    transparent product decisions.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Value:</b> Prioritize features that solve important customer problems or significantly improve the user experience.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Business Impact:</b> Consider how features contribute to revenue, growth, customer retention, efficiency, or strategic goals.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Development Effort:</b> Compare expected value against the time, resources, and complexity required for implementation.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Strategic Alignment:</b> Ensure prioritized features support the product vision and broader business strategy.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Technical Feasibility:</b> Consider architecture, technology limitations, dependencies, and implementation complexity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Risk and Uncertainty:</b> Account for potential technical, market, operational, and delivery risks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Data-Driven Decisions:</b> Use customer feedback, product analytics, research, and business data to support prioritization decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant prioritization image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

