            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>How to Measure Feature Prioritization Effectiveness</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Measuring prioritization effectiveness helps product teams determine
                    whether the features selected for development are actually producing
                    meaningful customer and business outcomes.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Feature Adoption:</b> Measure how frequently customers use newly delivered features.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Impact:</b> Evaluate whether prioritized features solve important customer problems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Business Outcomes:</b> Track revenue, retention, conversion, efficiency, or other expected business improvements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Delivery Performance:</b> Compare planned development effort and timelines with actual results.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Roadmap Success:</b> Evaluate whether completed roadmap initiatives contribute to strategic product objectives.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Stakeholder Alignment:</b> Assess whether prioritization decisions create better alignment across product and delivery teams.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant analytics image here when available. *@
